vidscribe (0.1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Initial release.
  * Turn a video URL (anything yt-dlp supports) or a local audio/video file
    into a timed transcript with whisper.cpp.
  * Output formats txt, srt, vtt and json (-f); --json-full adds per-token
    timing.
  * Accept several URLs/files in one call; a failing source does not stop
    the others, the exit status is non-zero.
  * Select model (-m), language (-l) and output directory (-o).
  * Download models once and verify them against the published SHA-256.
  * Add -c to pass browser cookies to yt-dlp for login-walled videos.
  * Add --keep-video to also save the merged downloaded media file.
  * Add --cpu to disable the GPU and -V/--version.
  * Never overwrite existing transcripts (title-2.*, title-3.*, ...).
  * Sanitize downloaded titles for use as file names.
  * Ship a man page, Makefile, CI and tests with a CC BY-SA speech fixture.

 -- Johannes Sood <info@somestrangedays.dev>  Mon, 12 Oct 2026 01:08:47 +0200
